One of my more promising wizards just met his rather annoying demise.
A bookstore on Dlvl 4 had given me quite a few nice spells (remove
curse, cause fear, haste self, fireball, invisibility). But there wasn't
much good armor in the upper levels, so my AC was only 4, and I hadn't found
a single dagger, so I was relying on force bolt and my quarterstaff, and 
therefore decided to head to the mines to find some, and hopefully a coaligned
altar (one of my starting spellbooks was create monster). First mines
level I kill a couple of gnomes for some daggers, and then a bolt of fire
comes from nowhere (I knew trying to do the level without a source of
light was a mistake, but...). One move back towards the upstairs and 
I'm toast, thanks to the hobbit who now came into view, wand blazing.
Sigh. At least less typical than the proverbial gnome with a /oD, 
I suppose.


